  <notes>
    2026-10-04: BLOCKED on escalation trigger 3 before any code edit. `/conflict-check` found that
    unified-access-control-r2 task 161 (#1100), commits 7f9159027 and 0f8cc61ea, merged and pushed to
    origin/integ/uac-r2-batch4 but not on master, already authorizes /send and /send-bulk. It checks Read on
    every attachment, AppendTo on every association, sends one 403 code for unknown and denied ids, fails
    closed, and checks the bulk request once. It reuses existing evaluators through
    CommunicationRecordAuthorizationFilter. UAC task 146 also edits ArchiveOutboundAttachmentsAsync but does
    not fix the archive bug. Archive bug confirmed at CommunicationService.cs:2330/2342. The fix should use
    the SOURCE document's own drive and item ids, not ArchiveContainerId. Recommendation: do not deploy the
    Word Email tab until UAC-r2 is on master; re-scope 097 to the archive fix (after UAC lands) and the live
    check. All acceptance criteria are OPEN. Details:
    notes/097-communications-send-authorization.md.
    OWNER DECISION 2026-10-04 (option 1): "yes we can follow your recommendation - ensure we have this fully documented". The authorization is UAC-r2 task 161's (one implementation). The Word Email tab (096) is held off by a build setting (ADDIN_EMAIL_TAB_ENABLED, default off) until 161 is on master and deployed. 097 is re-scoped to the archive fix (after UAC-r2 task 146 lands on the same lines) plus the live checks. Full record: notes/097-communications-send-authorization.md section 6.
  </notes>

